## Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- **Python 3.14** or higher
- **Virtual Environment** tool (`venv`)
- **Docker** (optional, for containerized execution)

---

### Local Setup Instructions

1. **Clone the repository:**
   ```bash
   git clone [https://github.com/your-username/sector-rotation-ml.git](https://github.com/your-username/sector-rotation-ml.git)
   cd sector-rotation-ml
   ```

2. **Initialize Environment and Install Dependencies:**

```
make setup
```
(Creates a .venv directory, upgrades pip, installs the package in editable mode with development extras, and sets up pre-commit hooks).

3. **Configure Environment Variables:**

Copy the example environment template and adjust settings as needed:
```
cp .env.example .env
```
